{
  "_doc": "Robot types. requires_research = research node id needed before the type can be built (absent = unlocked from the start). [ui2] parts = Parts for the first robot of the type (with cost in cubes; cubes grow x1.35 and parts x1.2 per robot owned). recipe = flavour only now (the part types a robot is made of; nothing is consumed). stats = Mk I base values. tiers = visual/stat tiers: mult multiplies all work stats; requires_core_rarity = unused since [ui2] (Mk steps cost cubes + Fleet.TIER_PARTS). Fleet upgrades apply to every robot of the type. [M3-19] Robots and what they build cost Parts only (cubes pay for Lumi's own upgrades, base levels and builds); the Scoopie's 10 Parts is the accepted proposal's first-robot price. part_drop: the chance, by waste type, that a take of salvage.ref_take units holds a piece worth stripping (one robot part) on a hex of salvage.ref_work units; the chance is scaled so a hex yields the same parts however heavy it is. salvage: Parts are scarce here (design spec section 14: 0 to 3 a hex, from Lumi's own hands only): rarity_parts = Parts one found robot part pays by rarity (rusty to legendary), buried_per_hex = buried parts a hex holds on average (about one in three hexes), ref_take and ref_work as above. With these a hex yields about 0.8 Parts: half buried, half stripped. fragment_parts = Parts a Maker Fragment pays.",
